  "Question": "A car travels \\(120\\) miles from \\(A\\) to \\(B\\) at \\(30\\) miles per hour but returns the same distance at \\(40\\) miles per hour. The average speed for the round trip is closest to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(33\\) mph",
    "B": "\\(34\\) mph",
    "C": "\\(35\\) mph",
    "D": "\\(36\\) mph",
    "E": "\\(37\\) mph"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Average speed is total distance divided by total travel time. First find the time for each leg:\n\\[\n\\frac{120}{30}=4\\text{ hours},\\qquad \\frac{120}{40}=3\\text{ hours}.\n\\]\nThe car travels \\(240\\) miles in \\(7\\) hours, so its average speed is\n\\[\n\\frac{240}{7}=34\\frac{2}{7}\\approx34.29\\text{ mph}.\n\\]\nThis lies between \\(34\\) and \\(34.5\\) mph, so the closest listed speed is \\(34\\) mph, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
